	(paper "A3")
	(title_block
		(title "Bay Station")
		(comment 1 "UWB rescue locator -- bay station: nRF9151 + BT840 bridge + 4x DW3210")
	)
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "DATA FLOW\ntag --UWB CH5--> A0..A3 (DW3210) --SPI--> nRF9151 --UART--> BT840 --BLE--> laptop\n                                              nRF9151 --LTE-M--> uplink (backend open)\nTCXO --> 1:4 buffer --> XTI of A0..A3 (equal length; 1 cm skew ~ 10 cm error at 10 m)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "12bd9bda-4fdb-4408-ace5-5049dba0b886")
	)
	(text "HOST: Nordic nRF9151 SiP (LTE-M/NB-IoT modem + GNSS + Cortex-M33 app core) on the Connectivity\nsheet. It owns everything: the UWB SPI bus, the I2C sensor bus, the status LEDs, the debug UART,\nand the LTE-M uplink. GNSS is the nRF9151's own receiver, time-shared with LTE (MAX-M10S removed).\n\nBLE BRIDGE: Fanstel BT840 (nRF52840), demoted to a UART BLE bridge to the laptop (BRIDGE_TXD/RXD/\nRTS/CTS/IRQ, RESET_BLE_N). The nRF9151 has no Bluetooth radio -- same split as Nordic Thingy:91 X.\n\nUWB: 4x Qorvo DW3210 on ONE shared SPI bus and ONE shared 38.4 MHz TCXO (1:4 buffer, Clock Distribution),\nantennas remote on 1-2 m coax via SMA (CH5, 6489.6 MHz). The anchors are NOT peers:\n    A0 = CENTRE anchor (UWB_CS0_N / UWB_IRQ0 / UWB_CLK0): two-way ranging with the tag -> RANGE\n    A1-A3 = OUTER anchors: TDoA against A0 on the same tag frame -> DIRECTION\n    range + direction = 3D position, relative to the array frame (docs/positioning.md)\n\nGEOREFERENCE: nRF9151 GNSS (where) + LIS3MDL heading and LIS2DH tilt on Orientation (which way).\nPOWER: MCP73871 charger/power-path + MAX17048 gauge (Power BMS) -> +VSYS -> TPS62A02 +3V3 and\n+VBAT_LTE (Regulation). Cross-sheet net names are fixed by docs/net-contract.md."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.7 1.7)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "615a5fc9-9773-4fbc-82a5-2b2faa2778e9")
	)
	(text "HOST + RADIOS + SENSORS"
